# Genesis Dossier — {{product-name}}

> **How to use:** instantiated in F0 to `product/99-records/genesis.md`
> (`workflows/W00-project-kickoff.md`) and gains **one line at the close of each phase** — it
> is part of the gate (`checklists/definition-of-done.md`). A project that was not born with it
> instantiates it midway (`playbooks/sync-framework.md` step 6b, or adopting via
> `workflows/W00-project-kickoff.md` §Adopting in a product that already exists): measurement
> starts on that date, and phases already closed get marked "not measured" — never
> reconstructed. In F9 the unit of measurement becomes the evolution (§Evolutions). It is the
> instrument that measures the framework's promise ("each product cheaper and better than the
> previous one"): without these numbers, the improvement is conviction; with them, it is the
> curve in `knowledge/learning-curve.md`. Honest, approximate numbers are worth more than empty
> fields — estimating is allowed, inventing is not (`knowledge/permanent-rules.md`).

